WEBVTT

00:00:01.044 --> 00:00:02.145
Hey, hey, Solty.

00:00:02.145 --> 00:00:04.014
What is it, Miss Kasha?

00:00:04.014 --> 00:00:06.683
You hear about it everywhere these days.

00:00:06.683 --> 00:00:09.352
But do you really know
what resemble technology is?

00:00:09.352 --> 00:00:10.487
I do not know.

00:00:10.487 --> 00:00:12.789
You should!

00:00:12.789 --> 00:00:14.624
Oh, you're hopeless.

00:00:14.624 --> 00:00:17.661
I'll explain what it is,
just for you, Solty.

00:00:17.661 --> 00:00:19.596
Please do.

00:00:19.596 --> 00:00:24.100
Simply put, resemble technology
refers to mechanical prosthetics

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.704
and it's a technology that
developed a lot after Blast Fall.

00:00:27.704 --> 00:00:28.905
Wow!

00:00:28.905 --> 00:00:33.443
But you know how resemble technology
gives people abnormal strengths?

00:00:33.443 --> 00:00:36.713
So, it's come to be used
in crimes quite a bit, too.

00:00:36.713 --> 00:00:38.415
That is terrible.

00:00:38.415 --> 00:00:39.482
But there are people

00:00:39.482 --> 00:00:43.620
who want to use resemble technology
for the good of the world, too!

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.955
Wow!

00:00:44.955 --> 00:00:47.524
And those people are
the Resemble Rescue Team!

00:00:47.524 --> 00:00:50.193
Even in places where you
can't work with large machines,

00:00:50.193 --> 00:00:52.562
with the power of resemble technology,
it's no problem for them!

00:00:52.562 --> 00:00:54.564
That is wonderful!

00:00:54.564 --> 00:00:57.534
New applications continue
to be found for resemble technology.

00:00:57.534 --> 00:00:59.903
So, that's it for this week.

00:00:59.903 --> 00:01:02.505
Well, then, everyone, see you next week!

00:01:02.505 --> 00:01:04.063
Next week!

00:01:08.545 --> 00:01:11.173
Well, that's the way things are.

00:01:18.154 --> 00:01:21.057
Owowowowow...

00:01:21.057 --> 00:01:23.493
Are you all right, Miss Rose?

00:01:23.493 --> 00:01:27.263
Well, yeah.

00:01:27.263 --> 00:01:28.865
Just barely.

00:01:28.865 --> 00:01:31.534
But...

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:35.839
The hole we fell through is blocked now...

00:01:35.839 --> 00:01:37.898
I know...

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:47.250
Nee ima made shiritakatta
otogi-banashi no tsuzuki

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:53.712
Eien ni owaranai
shiawase nara kono te de

00:01:55.425 --> 00:02:05.402
Bokura wa marude ichimai-chigai
no guuzen o sagashiatte

00:02:05.402 --> 00:02:07.570
Meguriatta

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:15.645
Kimi ga itsuka
nomikonda sono kotoba yori

00:02:15.645 --> 00:02:24.587
Zutto iezu ni
itekureteta yasashisa o

00:02:24.587 --> 00:02:31.561
Shinjitai to ima omounda

00:02:31.561 --> 00:02:39.302
Nee kono saki wa doko made mo
fuan to tonari-awase

00:02:39.302 --> 00:02:45.708
Nakusu mono ga nakatta
bokutachi wa mou inai

00:02:45.708 --> 00:02:53.416
Nee ima made shiranakatta
otogi-banashi no tsuzuki

00:02:53.416 --> 00:02:59.589
Eien ni owaranai
shiawase nara kono te de

00:02:59.589 --> 00:03:03.491
Tsumikasanete
yuku mono

00:03:09.532 --> 00:03:14.128
"Treasure & Rescue"

00:03:20.475 --> 00:03:22.845
Roy!

00:03:22.845 --> 00:03:24.346
What's going on?

00:03:24.346 --> 00:03:28.283
Is it true that Solty
and Rose fell underground?

00:03:28.283 --> 00:03:29.384
Yeah.

00:03:29.384 --> 00:03:31.909
We were in the middle
of chasing a bounty.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.070
Then we have to hurry up and rescue them!

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:50.706
Oh, you've got nothing to worry about.

00:03:50.706 --> 00:03:54.710
Working in places like this,
where large machines can't get into,

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:58.280
is exactly why we,
the Resemble Rescue Team, exist.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:00.182
We'll rescue those two,
no matter what.

00:04:00.182 --> 00:04:01.416
You swear?

00:04:01.416 --> 00:04:03.218
Yeah, we swear!

00:04:03.218 --> 00:04:05.187
So there you have it.

00:04:05.187 --> 00:04:07.856
We better settle in
for the long haul.

00:04:07.856 --> 00:04:09.758
Aren't you worried?

00:04:09.758 --> 00:04:12.556
Those two won't die so easily.

00:04:16.064 --> 00:04:18.225
This feels so good!

00:04:21.103 --> 00:04:23.970
Um, Miss Rose?

00:04:24.907 --> 00:04:25.874
What is it?

00:04:25.874 --> 00:04:27.609
Why a shower?

00:04:27.609 --> 00:04:30.178
We got covered in dust.

00:04:30.178 --> 00:04:34.249
The first thing to do
is to wash it off in a shower.

00:04:34.249 --> 00:04:36.151
It's the basics of being a girl.

00:04:36.151 --> 00:04:39.882
- I see...
- Come on, wash yourself thoroughly, too!

00:04:50.132 --> 00:04:51.667
Um...

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:52.601
What?

00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:54.903
I am not sure that is quite proper...

00:04:54.903 --> 00:04:58.607
It's no big deal.
No one's watching anyway.

00:04:58.607 --> 00:05:00.075
The basics of being a girl...

00:05:00.075 --> 00:05:01.440
What was that?

00:05:04.112 --> 00:05:08.016
It's no good.
I can't open it by myself.

00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:12.120
By the way, what in the world is this place?

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.690
This place? It's the old city.

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:16.858
The old city?

00:05:16.858 --> 00:05:20.362
Yup. I don't know when they were built,

00:05:20.362 --> 00:05:24.232
but there are several cities
like this underground.

00:05:24.232 --> 00:05:27.202
As you can see,
no one lives here anymore,

00:05:27.202 --> 00:05:30.772
but they've become nice
playground areas for kids.

00:05:30.772 --> 00:05:35.310
Though, I hear a lot of it
is getting rickety, since it's not used.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.245
I see.

00:05:37.245 --> 00:05:40.916
Never mind all that.
Help me open this thing.

00:05:40.916 --> 00:05:44.419
But is that not wrong to do?

00:05:44.419 --> 00:05:47.489
No one's around, so it doesn't matter.

00:05:47.489 --> 00:05:49.191
Come on, hurry up.

00:05:49.191 --> 00:05:51.994
I'm getting a little hungry, too.

00:05:51.994 --> 00:05:54.696
Then let us hurry up
and find a way out.

00:05:54.696 --> 00:05:56.898
I am sure Mr. Roy
is worried about us as well.

00:05:56.898 --> 00:05:58.700
Worried?

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.235
That old man?

00:06:00.235 --> 00:06:02.237
No way he's worried!

00:06:02.237 --> 00:06:04.406
He is worried.

00:06:04.406 --> 00:06:05.974
You really think so?

00:06:05.974 --> 00:06:09.311
He is worried!

00:06:09.311 --> 00:06:11.179
I am telling you he is!

00:06:11.179 --> 00:06:14.282
All right. All right, already.

00:06:14.282 --> 00:06:16.716
Hurry up and open this thing.

00:06:17.886 --> 00:06:19.521
But...

00:06:19.521 --> 00:06:21.323
We're going to look
for a way out, right?

00:06:21.323 --> 00:06:24.026
We don't even know
where it's going to be.

00:06:24.026 --> 00:06:28.296
We have to start by
securing a supply of food.

00:06:28.296 --> 00:06:29.888
Come on, hurry up.

00:06:31.466 --> 00:06:33.161
I understand.

00:06:37.205 --> 00:06:38.729
Good work!

00:06:58.727 --> 00:07:02.030
Say, can't they do this any faster?

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:03.899
The sun's going to set at this rate.

00:07:03.899 --> 00:07:07.858
But this kind of work
always takes time...

00:07:15.277 --> 00:07:18.576
I have to say, even I'm getting
tired of drinking coffee.

00:07:27.923 --> 00:07:29.458
Sheesh!

00:07:29.458 --> 00:07:32.552
There's nothing of value here at all!

00:07:38.533 --> 00:07:42.204
Um, what are you doing?

00:07:42.204 --> 00:07:45.974
Well, isn't it obvious?

00:07:45.974 --> 00:07:48.977
Treasure hunting.

00:07:48.977 --> 00:07:51.213
Miss Rose...

00:07:51.213 --> 00:07:55.617
Mr. Roy is worried about us, so we
were going to hurry up and get out.

00:07:55.617 --> 00:07:57.285
I know that.

00:07:57.285 --> 00:08:00.422
That's why we've kept moving
in an upwards direction.

00:08:00.422 --> 00:08:02.424
I'm just doing this on the way.

00:08:02.424 --> 00:08:05.760
Especially since this area doesn't
seem to have been ransacked yet.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:07.429
Miss Rose!

00:08:07.429 --> 00:08:09.631
Besides...

00:08:09.631 --> 00:08:12.367
You sometimes find things like this.

00:08:12.367 --> 00:08:15.003
What is this? A map?

00:08:15.003 --> 00:08:16.938
Well, something like that.

00:08:16.938 --> 00:08:21.409
Anyway, what language is this?!
I can't read it at all!

00:08:21.409 --> 00:08:25.038
I'm sure it has to be
a map of this area...

00:08:26.948 --> 00:08:30.519
Power distribution room...
Linen room...

00:08:30.519 --> 00:08:35.924
Laundry room... Afforestation
promotion room... Medical room...

00:08:35.924 --> 00:08:37.325
You can read that?

00:08:37.325 --> 00:08:40.662
What? Oh, yes...

00:08:40.662 --> 00:08:42.330
Why?

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.230
I do not know.

00:08:46.067 --> 00:08:49.104
Well, who cares?
Good work, Solty.

00:08:49.104 --> 00:08:51.806
So, where do you think we're
most likely to find treasure?

00:08:51.806 --> 00:08:54.042
Miss Rose.

00:08:54.042 --> 00:08:55.737
I was just kidding.

00:08:57.179 --> 00:08:58.680
But you know,

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:03.118
I don't think you need to be
so worried about that old man.

00:09:03.118 --> 00:09:05.287
Just because he's your stepfather...

00:09:05.287 --> 00:09:07.556
What is a "step" father?

00:09:07.556 --> 00:09:11.226
It means that he's
not your real father.

00:09:11.226 --> 00:09:13.361
Mr. Roy is my father.

00:09:13.361 --> 00:09:16.694
No, well, yeah, but...

00:09:30.478 --> 00:09:33.648
What do you like about him
that makes you care so much?

00:09:33.648 --> 00:09:34.916
What do I like?

00:09:34.916 --> 00:09:37.919
Well, Mr. Roy has helped
me out in various ways

00:09:37.919 --> 00:09:43.380
and he helped you when you wanted
to avenge your friend, too.

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:49.698
Helped me, huh?

00:09:49.698 --> 00:09:51.466
Does that count as helping me?

00:09:51.466 --> 00:09:54.035
I do think it counts.

00:09:54.035 --> 00:09:55.559
I wonder...

00:10:04.679 --> 00:10:09.951
More importantly, when are we
going to get to the surface?!

00:10:09.951 --> 00:10:12.078
Calm down, Miss Rose.

00:10:16.491 --> 00:10:19.794
Hey, haven't you gotten
to the bottom yet?!

00:10:19.794 --> 00:10:22.097
Kasha.

00:10:22.097 --> 00:10:26.401
They're all working hard, okay?

00:10:26.401 --> 00:10:27.925
But...

00:10:31.339 --> 00:10:33.441
What?! You found someone?!

00:10:33.441 --> 00:10:35.432
All right, pull it up!

00:10:46.988 --> 00:10:48.123
Who is he?

00:10:48.123 --> 00:10:50.956
He's the bounty we were after.

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:53.454
Captain!

00:11:20.455 --> 00:11:21.323
What?

00:11:21.323 --> 00:11:22.657
Are you singing?

00:11:22.657 --> 00:11:24.993
Oh, sort of.

00:11:24.993 --> 00:11:26.995
It's like a habit of mine.

00:11:26.995 --> 00:11:30.465
Somehow, it just... makes me relax.

00:11:30.465 --> 00:11:32.092
I see...

00:11:45.914 --> 00:11:47.438
You suck at it.

00:11:59.627 --> 00:12:03.431
That's the last of our food and drink.

00:12:03.431 --> 00:12:06.134
Oh, man, I'm tired.

00:12:06.134 --> 00:12:09.671
Just how far do we have to go up
before we can get out?

00:12:09.671 --> 00:12:13.475
We will get out.
I am certain.

00:12:13.475 --> 00:12:16.277
You're so laid back.

00:12:16.277 --> 00:12:18.980
Let us keep it up, Miss Rose.

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:22.550
More like, if that old man's worried,

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:25.019
he should hurry up and come rescue us.

00:12:25.019 --> 00:12:25.887
Right?

00:12:25.887 --> 00:12:30.492
He is sure to be trying
to rescue us right this moment.

00:12:30.492 --> 00:12:31.826
You think so?

00:12:31.826 --> 00:12:33.728
I am certain of it.

00:12:33.728 --> 00:12:35.330
You really think so?

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:37.799
I am certain.

00:12:37.799 --> 00:12:39.667
Maybe so.

00:12:39.667 --> 00:12:41.436
Yes.

00:12:41.436 --> 00:12:45.907
But my pride won't allow me
to just wait for that to come

00:12:45.907 --> 00:12:49.944
and there's no knowing
what kind of flack I'll get if I did.

00:12:49.944 --> 00:12:52.747
Let's go, Solty.

00:12:52.747 --> 00:12:53.771
Right!

00:12:59.421 --> 00:13:01.923
Just how long are you going to take?!

00:13:01.923 --> 00:13:05.193
Were you lying when you said
you'd rescue them?!

00:13:05.193 --> 00:13:07.962
I wasn't lying.
Give us a little longer.

00:13:07.962 --> 00:13:10.265
Everyone on the team
is working relentlessly, too.

00:13:10.265 --> 00:13:12.893
- But...
- Calm down, Kasha.

00:13:17.205 --> 00:13:20.072
Is there anything I can do?

00:13:44.599 --> 00:13:46.260
Ow...

00:14:06.955 --> 00:14:08.217
Roy...

00:14:09.557 --> 00:14:12.890
He can't stay calm unless
he's doing something, too...

00:14:33.715 --> 00:14:35.910
Evacuate! All hands evacuate!

00:14:47.262 --> 00:14:50.231
Hey, was anyone injured?

00:14:50.231 --> 00:14:51.666
Tom and Orlando were.

00:14:51.666 --> 00:14:53.429
Take them to the hospital right away.

00:15:01.142 --> 00:15:02.541
Kasha...

00:15:10.919 --> 00:15:12.687
Don't be ridiculous!

00:15:12.687 --> 00:15:14.622
You're going to stop working?!

00:15:14.622 --> 00:15:16.457
The foundation here is unstable.

00:15:16.457 --> 00:15:19.127
It's already a difficult
enough area to work in.

00:15:19.127 --> 00:15:21.329
When you consider this
situation on top of that,

00:15:21.329 --> 00:15:24.432
further work is unthinkable!

00:15:24.432 --> 00:15:26.935
Roy!

00:15:26.935 --> 00:15:30.305
At this rate, we'll end up
with more secondary casualties.

00:15:30.305 --> 00:15:34.876
If we could find another way in,
the story would be different,

00:15:34.876 --> 00:15:36.010
but I'm sorry.

00:15:36.010 --> 00:15:39.380
I've got the lives
of my men to think of, too.

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:42.016
I'll do it, even if I have to do it alone.

00:15:42.016 --> 00:15:43.217
Wait, Roy!

00:15:43.217 --> 00:15:46.414
What the heck do you think
you can do alone, Mister?

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:50.291
Who are you people?

00:15:50.291 --> 00:15:52.026
I called them here.

00:15:52.026 --> 00:15:54.896
They're Rose's older brothers.

00:15:54.896 --> 00:15:57.465
Hey, you there, Mister.

00:15:57.465 --> 00:16:01.235
You said the story'd be different
if there was another way in, right?

00:16:01.235 --> 00:16:02.370
Yeah.

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:03.838
We can find that way.

00:16:03.838 --> 00:16:07.809
It was so old, we had a little trouble
getting a hold of it, though.

00:16:07.809 --> 00:16:11.040
This contains the map data
of the underground city beneath us.

00:16:12.947 --> 00:16:15.083
Is it really under here?

00:16:15.083 --> 00:16:16.751
There's no mistake about it.

00:16:16.751 --> 00:16:21.589
There should be a large air purification
circulation vent under here.

00:16:21.589 --> 00:16:23.758
The diameter is roughly 4 meters.

00:16:23.758 --> 00:16:26.694
- Is that too small?
- No, that's plenty.

00:16:26.694 --> 00:16:29.430
You guys, tear up this concrete!

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:30.397
Yes, Sir!

00:16:31.532 --> 00:16:33.801
Will you help us, too?

00:16:33.801 --> 00:16:35.234
That goes without asking.

00:16:38.439 --> 00:16:39.941
What's this?

00:16:39.941 --> 00:16:44.412
This is an external plug
used to access the system inside.

00:16:44.412 --> 00:16:46.903
This is where I come in.

00:16:48.249 --> 00:16:51.219
The underground city
was built a long time ago,

00:16:51.219 --> 00:16:55.490
so the standard connection
cable is different, too.

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:57.583
But we've got one.

00:17:01.396 --> 00:17:02.597
Can you do it?

00:17:02.597 --> 00:17:04.531
I'm an old hand at this.

00:17:10.438 --> 00:17:11.239
What is it?

00:17:11.239 --> 00:17:14.709
Well, the system inside is unstable.

00:17:14.709 --> 00:17:17.278
I wonder if it's out of whack
because it's too old.

00:17:17.278 --> 00:17:19.047
Does it look like a no-go?

00:17:19.047 --> 00:17:20.882
It's not completely dead.

00:17:20.882 --> 00:17:22.050
I think I can do it.

00:17:22.050 --> 00:17:25.042
Okay, I'm going to access
the internal information.

00:17:28.656 --> 00:17:30.425
What's all that red?

00:17:30.425 --> 00:17:32.660
Oh, man, is this for real?

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:34.218
There's a fire down there.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:49.977
What about the two down there?
Can't you tell where Solty and Rose are?

00:17:49.977 --> 00:17:52.980
Hold on. I'm checking that right now.

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:54.215
Damn it!

00:17:54.215 --> 00:17:56.581
It's no good. The system
of sensors is dead.

00:17:57.919 --> 00:17:59.580
What the hell is going on here?!

00:18:02.123 --> 00:18:04.258
There's no doubt that it's there.

00:18:04.258 --> 00:18:06.928
The fact it's covered with
a steel plate proves it.

00:18:06.928 --> 00:18:10.765
Once that's removed,
the large vent is certain to be there.

00:18:10.765 --> 00:18:13.434
All right! Everyone get
to removing this thing!

00:18:13.434 --> 00:18:17.638
Damn it! Why aren't
the sprinklers operating?!

00:18:17.638 --> 00:18:20.575
Hey, you gotta be kidding me!

00:18:20.575 --> 00:18:24.033
At this rate, the fire will light up
the gas tanks in the fuel room.

00:18:32.854 --> 00:18:33.988
It's settled down.

00:18:33.988 --> 00:18:36.090
That was a big tremor!

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:38.159
Damn it! An explosion
big enough to do that...

00:18:38.159 --> 00:18:40.294
What kind of effect
did it have on the inside?

00:18:40.294 --> 00:18:41.727
Mom...

00:18:42.797 --> 00:18:44.321
Heave!

00:18:47.902 --> 00:18:51.139
Hey, this isn't how you said it'd be.

00:18:51.139 --> 00:18:54.075
It's the system's internal shutter.

00:18:54.075 --> 00:18:55.176
Can you open it?

00:18:55.176 --> 00:18:56.302
I'll try it.

00:18:57.512 --> 00:18:58.346
Wha...

00:18:58.346 --> 00:19:00.181
Don't mess with me, damn you!

00:19:00.181 --> 00:19:01.783
It's one thing after another!

00:19:01.783 --> 00:19:02.784
What's wrong?

00:19:02.784 --> 00:19:06.721
The remaining oxygen in the
underground city is almost gone!

00:19:06.721 --> 00:19:08.422
Hurry up and open the shutter!

00:19:08.422 --> 00:19:10.014
I know!

00:19:17.865 --> 00:19:21.302
Damn it! The system went down.

00:19:21.302 --> 00:19:23.702
You can't open the shutter?

00:19:24.839 --> 00:19:26.306
But then...

00:19:37.318 --> 00:19:38.376
Damn it!

00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:43.124
Move aside. We'll handle this somehow.

00:19:43.124 --> 00:19:44.959
The electric saw!
Bring over the electric saw!

00:19:44.959 --> 00:19:47.762
Captain, let's pry it open with our arms!

00:19:47.762 --> 00:19:51.399
I don't care how we do it!
Just break it open!

00:19:51.399 --> 00:19:52.889
Damn it!

00:19:54.602 --> 00:19:55.728
Damn it!

00:19:59.106 --> 00:20:03.065
Am I going to lose someone again?

00:20:04.745 --> 00:20:06.076
Again...

00:20:07.715 --> 00:20:08.909
Roy...

00:20:14.255 --> 00:20:15.656
What's that?

00:20:15.656 --> 00:20:17.089
This sound...

00:20:22.663 --> 00:20:23.925
Evacuate!

00:20:47.221 --> 00:20:49.451
S-Solty!

00:20:52.593 --> 00:20:54.891
Thank goodness!
You're alive!

00:20:58.532 --> 00:20:59.967
Rose.

00:20:59.967 --> 00:21:01.229
Rose!

00:21:07.108 --> 00:21:09.576
Huh? Brother?

00:21:14.448 --> 00:21:16.150
You're amazing.

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:18.352
How did you break that open?

00:21:18.352 --> 00:21:20.411
Uh, well...

00:21:31.999 --> 00:21:33.762
We're going home.

00:21:53.618 --> 00:21:58.390
Hareta hi no kouen

00:21:58.390 --> 00:22:01.326
Miageta sora ni

00:22:01.326 --> 00:22:09.734
Kiesou ni natta chiisana
Little Cloud

00:22:12.604 --> 00:22:17.375
Kaze ni mi o makasete

00:22:17.375 --> 00:22:20.312
Jiyuu ni ikiru

00:22:20.312 --> 00:22:28.353
Sukoshi-zutsu
aruku watashi-tachi

00:22:28.353 --> 00:22:33.124
Onnaji dane

00:22:33.124 --> 00:22:37.862
Taisetsu na jikan

00:22:37.862 --> 00:22:41.700
Deau tabi ni

00:22:41.700 --> 00:22:51.242
Hitori ja nai kono kimochi
yasashisa ni naru

00:22:51.242 --> 00:22:57.816
Dareka o shinjiru
yuuki ni kaete

00:22:57.816 --> 00:23:10.126
Kitto kono mama ano sora
no hate ni kieru mae ni

00:23:16.601 --> 00:23:19.337
I have something I am
looking forward to right now.

00:23:19.337 --> 00:23:21.506
Oh, you mean the old man's birthd-

00:23:21.506 --> 00:23:23.174
Oh, oh, oh!

00:23:23.174 --> 00:23:25.410
Next time, "Birthday Game".

00:23:25.410 --> 00:23:26.900
It is a secret.
